  "limitations": [
    "Simulated users: speech in synthetic rooms with DEMAND noise, not microphone captures. The simulator makes no clipped, silent or non-finite takes, so A1-A4 cannot fire, and no user has custom settings.",
    "Current settings are always the factory Preset(); real users' current settings are unknown. This is the main limitation, and a false refusal here is a false refusal against defaults.",
    "18 speakers (48 of 54 users male), so intervals are wide; more realizations per speaker do not narrow them.",
    "Known limits unchanged: the tonal check is nearly blind below 1 kHz; Auto-EQ's Adaptive inputs saturate for real voices; in reverberant captures noise is judged by pauses of at least 600 ms from speech.",
    "A clause that cannot be measured is reported as a lower and an upper bound; the headline treats it as worse.",
    "Verification hears the first 10 s of the evaluation capture and the judge the whole 20 s, so for C1 and C2 the judge overlaps the evidence; the last 10 s is the sensitivity reading.",
    "Sibilant loss is read against the noisy input as the product's own dulling advice reads it, so it includes what the whole chain does to consonants, not only the withheld step.",
    "The tuner's upper bound renders the gate and suppressor stage alone and omits the tone, sibilant and overload clauses; it can only overstate.",
    "The tone of a B5 step is the optimizer's validated fit before the abstention and the headroom scaling.",
    "For B1 the judged object is the proposal had validation passed, a counterfactual the product discards; the B2-B6 flags of a B1 user come from that run.",
    "The tuner's best non-incumbent candidate may be one the tuner scored worse than the incumbent; the cause 'margin' then means that the tuner kept the incumbent without a holdout, not that the candidate came close.",
    "The tuner's runtime gate reads wall-clock time, so its candidates depend on the machine's load; each row records every candidate's failed gates and runtime factor.",
    "A veto fired by fewer than 7 users is underpowered: with 54 users in 18 clusters of 3 the trigger cannot fire for it even if every firing were false and from a different speaker, so its silence says nothing.",
    "df.dll is a local build whose SHA-256 differs from release-assets.json; both are recorded under release_assets."
  ],
